  "editorReview": {
    "text": "This chronicle offers a compelling re-examination of the Berlin Airlift, successfully framing the 'paper machine' of logistics as an active historical protagonist rather than a passive record. The argument finds its most potent form in the middle chapters, where meticulous archival evidence—such as the analysis of priority lists and manifests in Chapter 19—drives the narrative with precision and conceptual force. However, the structural discipline falters towards the end, where the rich, document-specific texture gives way to more generic strategic analysis. A noticeable repetition in chapter",
